  <data name="Category_61_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>يُعد تصنيف الروايات من الأدوات النقدية والفنية التي تهدف إلى تنظيم هذا الشكل الأدبي الطويل والمعقد وفق موضوعاته وأساليبه وبنيته الفنية، وتُعرّف الرواية بأنها سرد نثري طويل يتناول تجربة إنسانية مركبة من خلال شخصيات متعددة وأحداث متشابكة، ويعتمد تصنيف الروايات على معايير متعددة مثل النوع الأدبي، حيث نجد الروايات الواقعية التي ترصد الحياة اليومية، والروايات الرومانسية التي تركز على العلاقات العاطفية، والروايات البوليسية التي تدور حول الجريمة والتحقيق، والروايات التاريخية التي تستند إلى وقائع الماضي، والخيالية التي تبني عوالم غير مألوفة، كما يُمكن تصنيف الروايات حسب أسلوب السرد</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Author_5_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ahmed Abouelwafa</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Author_5_Bio" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ahmed Abouelwafa Mohamed(1962 – 2018) was an Egyptian author and physician, widely known as "The Godfather" of modern Arabic literature in horror, fantasy, and science fiction. He was the first contemporary Arab writer to explore the horror genre, becoming a cultural icon across the Arab world. His most famous book series include Ma Waraa Al Tabiaa (Metaphysics), Fantasia, and Safari. Tawfik’s work inspired generations of young readers and left a lasting legacy in modern Arabic literature.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Book_50_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>القادمون</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Book_50_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The long time has ended, and the long-awaited time has come. People are caught up in amusement and games, and temptations like pieces of a dark night. The earth has been decorated and prepared, and devils have ascended every pulpit. You do not know where to place your soul, or how to hold on to your religion. The fog of truth has covered the blackness of falsehood, and only the eye of your heart can see. Then the time for our departure has come, and people have prepared for the final temptation; the temptation of the end.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Category_86_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scary and inspiring</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Category_86_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In the Terrifying &amp; Inspiring section of Aseer Alkotb, the dread of darkness intertwines with sparks of hope, creating a mesmerizing world of contrasting emotions. Within its pages, you will encounter fear that takes your breath away, and inspiration that awakens hidden strength within you. It is a realm that leads you to the edge of fear only to reveal the depths of courage, leaving you suspended between the thrill of mystery and the pulse of life.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Author_23_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ahmed Khaled Mouwad </value>
  </data>
  <data name="Author_23_Bio" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ahmed Khaled Mouwad is a young writer passionate about exploring the realms of literature and thought, blending profound imagination with genuine human reflection in his works. His writings, ranging from inspiring reflections to thrilling tales, leave a lasting impact on readers. With a constant search for meaning, he believes that words hold the power to touch hearts and unlock new perspectives.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Book_51_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>root</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Book_51_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Passage is a book that takes you on a thrilling journey through corridors of fear and hope, where the narrow path becomes a symbol of life’s trials and challenges. Within its pages, you will encounter a blend of mystery and inspiration, reflecting the struggle between one’s inner self and the outer world. It is more than just a story; it is an invitation to discover the hidden strength within, as the dark passage transforms into a gateway to light and freedom.</value>
  </data>
